hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"10726","I am Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, narrated by Khaled, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, narrated by Abdul-Rahman, who said: Jami’ bin Shaddad informed me, on the authority of Safwan bin Mahrez, on the authority of Ibn Husayn, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is God and nothing else, and His throne was over the water, so it was written In the Reminder all things, then He created seven heavens.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10727","I am Muhammad bin Abdul Ala, from Khaled, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “None of my nation, whether Jew, or Christian, hears of me and then does not believe in me unless he enters Hell.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10728","I am Ahmad bin Abi Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Yazid bin Zurayi, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Safwan bin Mahrez, who said: Abdullah bin Omar said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying in an argument. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “The believer draws near to his Lord.” On the Day of Resurrection, He will place a shroud over him, then tell him of his sins: Do you know? He will say: My Lord knows best, until he has achieved what God wills. He said: And I have concealed it from you in this world, and I forgive it for you today. Then he will be given a record of his good deeds. As for the disbelievers, their Lord will call on The chief witnesses: These are those who lied about their Lord. Indeed, the curse of God is upon the wrongdoers. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10729","I am Abu Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Khalid bin Al-Harith, he said: On the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas: That the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ The believers will gather on the Day of Resurrection and say: If only we would intercede to our Lord and He would relieve us from this place we are in. Then they will go to Adam, peace be upon him. They say: You are the father of mankind. God created you with His hand, and His angels prostrated before you, so intercede for us with your Lord. Then He says: I am not here. And it will be mentioned to them and he will complain to them about the sin that befell him, and God will be ashamed of that. But go to Noah, for he is the first Messenger to be sent. God is to the people of the earth, and they call him, and he says: I am not there, and he remembers asking his Lord about what he has no knowledge, and he is ashamed of that. But go to Abraham, the friend of the Most Gracious, and they will go to him and he will say: I am not there, but go to Moses, a servant who spoke to God and gave him the Torah. So they come to him, and he says: I am not here, and he mentions killing a soul for another, but go to Jesus, the servant of God and His Messenger, and the word of God. And his spirit, so they come to him, and he says: I am not there, but go to Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him and all of God’s prophets, a servant whom God has forgiven. Whatever of his sins preceded and whatever came later, he said: “Then they will come to me and I will go.” Sa`id said: He mentioned this letter on the authority of Al-Hasan, so I would walk between Two generations of believers.” Then he returned to the hadith of Anas, and said: “So I will ask permission to my Lord, and He will give me permission. When I see him, I fall prostrating.” Then he will leave me as long as God wills, then it will be said: Raise, O Muhammad. Speak and you will be heard. Ask and it will be given to you. Intercede and you will be granted intercession. So I raise my head and praise Him. with praise that He would teach me, then I would intercede and He would set a punishment for me and admit them to Paradise. Then I would come back the second time, and when I saw him I fell prostrating, and he would leave me as long as he God wills that He will leave me, then it will be said: Raise, O Muhammad. Speak and you will be heard. Ask and it will be given to you. Intercede and you will be interceded. So I raise my head and praise Him with praise. He would teach me, then I would intercede, and he would set a punishment for me, so he would admit them to Paradise. Then I would return for the third time, and when I saw my Lord, I fell prostrating before Him, and He would leave me alone. Whatever God wills, then it will be said to me: Raise, O Muhammad, speak and you will be heard, ask and it will be given to you, intercede and you will be interceded, so I raise my head and praise Him with praise. He will teach me, then I will intercede, and he will set a limit for me and admit them to Paradise. Then I will return the fourth time and say: O Lord, there is none left except those whom the Qur’an has imprisoned.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10730","He said: Following this hadith, Qatada says: Anas bin Malik told us that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It comes out of Hell is the one who says: There is no god but God, and has in his heart a grain of good faith, and from the Fire will come out the one who says: There is no god but God, and there is In his heart is an atom’s weight of goodness, and from the Fire will emerge whoever has an atom’s weight of goodness in his heart.”"
"10731","I am Abdul-Hamid bin Muhammad, from Mukhlid, from Malik bin Mughul, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father. He said: The Messenger of God met him. May God bless him and grant him peace. So he entered the mosque and a man was reciting, and another was praying. He said: Then he went out the next night, and I met him and he took my hand. The mosque was illuminated, so we heard a voice and I said: O Messenger of God, do you see him as a hypocrite? He said: “No, but rather a believer who repents. Rather, he is a believer who repents.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10732","I am Abu Bakr bin Ali, narrated by Yahya bin Maeen, narrated by Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Burayd, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Indeed, God Almighty gives respite to the oppressor until when he takes him, he does not let him go or give him respite.” Then he recited: And thus is the punishment of your Lord when He takes the towns while they are unjust."
"10733","I am Ali bin Hajar, from Yazid bin Harun, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahb, and we are a partner, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahb, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated to us, and he is the truthful and trustworthy: “Indeed, the creation of Ibn Adam is gathered in his mother’s womb for forty, then he becomes a clot like that, then he becomes a lump like that, then he sends to him an angel who is written Four: his term, his work, his provision, whether he is miserable or happy.”"
"10734","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, from Ibn Abi Adi, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, and I am Ismail bin Masoud, on the authority of Yazid, who is Ibn Zurayi, and Bishr They said: Sulayman al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, that a man was kissed by a woman, so he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, asked him about her atonement, so God Almighty revealed: “And perform prayer at the ends of the day and at the end of the night. Indeed, good deeds go away.” Bad deeds. He said: O Messenger of God, what is this for? He said: “Rather, these are for those of my nation who do them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10735","I am Muhammad bin Hatim bin Naim, I am Suwayd, I am Abdullah, on the authority of Sharik, I am Othman bin Mawhib, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, on the authority of Abu Al-Yusr Bin Amr, he said: A woman came to him, and her husband had been sent by the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a mission, and she said to him: Sell me dates for a dirham. He said: So I said to her and she liked it: There are better dates in the house than these, so he went off with her and winked and kissed her, so he was frightened and then left. He met Abu Bakr and said to him: I have perished. He said: What is the matter with you? So he told him his story, and said to him: May I repent? He said: Yes, repent and do not repeat it, and do not tell anyone. Then he set off until he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him the story, and said: “You left behind a man from Muslims fighting in the name of God in this way? And I thought that I was one of the people of Hell, and that God would never forgive me, and the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, departed from me. May God bless him and grant him peace, until it was revealed to him: And perform prayer at the ends of the day and at the end of the night. Indeed, good deeds remove evil deeds. This is a reminder. For those who remember, so the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to me and recited them to me. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10736","I am Amr bin Ali, and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id narrated to me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: It was said: O Messenger of God, “Who is the most honorable to people?” He said: “The most pious of them.” They said: This is not what we ask you about. He said: “Joseph, the Prophet of God, the son of a Prophet.” “God, the son of God’s Prophet, the son of God’s friend.” They said: “We are not asking you about this.” He said: “You are asking me about the Arabs’ minerals, for their choice is in The pre-Islamic people are their choice in Islam if they understand it.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Muhammad ibn Bishr disagreed with him. I am Ahmad ibn Sulaiman, we are Muhammad ibn Bishr, from Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, the same. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10737","From us, Abu Dawud Suleiman bin Saif, from Yaqoub bin Ibrahim, from my father, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Urwa bin Al-Zubayr told me Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, Alqamah bin Waqqas, and Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he said The people of Ifk said what they said, so God cleared her of it. He said: And all of them narrated to me a group of her hadiths, and some of them were more aware of her hadiths than Some, and I confirmed his justification, and I learned from each man of them the hadith that he told me on the authority of Aisha, and some of their hadiths confirm others. And if some of them were more aware of it than others, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered and then sat down. He testified when he sat down, then said: “As for Then, O Aisha, I have heard such-and-such about you, so if you are innocent, God will exonerate you, even if you are guilty of a sin. So ask forgiveness from God and repent to Him, for if a servant confesses his sin and then repents, God will accept his repentance.” So I said to my father: Answer the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: By God, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I said to my mother: Answer the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, regarding what he said. She said: By God, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I said, as I am a young girl, no. I read from the Qur’an a lot: Indeed, by God, I know that you have heard this hadith until it settled in your souls and you believed in it. So if I say To you: I am innocent, do not believe me, and if I confessed to you something and God knows that I am innocent of it, you would believe me, for by God I find nothing wrong with it. For example, there is no one for you except Abu Yusuf when he said: Patience is great, and God is the one who seeks help in what you describe. By God, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not regret it. He continued his sitting until God Almighty revealed: “Indeed, those who brought falsehood are a group of you, all ten verses.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10738","I am Muhammad bin Salamah, I am Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha: that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.” Aisha said: O Messenger of God, if Abu Bakr took your place, he would not He could hear the people crying, so command Omar to lead the people in prayer. He said: “Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.” Aisha said: So I said to Hafsa: Tell him: When Abu Bakr stands in your place, the people will not hear your crying, so he ordered Omar to lead the people in prayer, and Hafsa did so, so he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Indeed, you are the companions of Joseph. Tell Abu Bakr so that he may lead the people in prayer.” Hafsa said: I would not have been injured. Good for you (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10739","I am Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem, I am Abdullah bin Muhammad, I am Juwayriyah bin Asma, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that Saeed Ibn Al-Musayyab, and Abu Ubaid told him, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “May God have mercy on Abraham, we More deserving of doubt than he. He said: “My Lord, show me how You bring the dead to life.” He said, “Do you not believe?” He said, “Yes, but so that my heart may be at peace.” And he said: “May God have mercy on Lot. He was sheltering in a harsh place, and if I had stayed in prison, Joseph would not have stayed. Then the caller came to me and I would have answered him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10740","I am Yusuf bin Issa, I am Al-Fadl, I am Muhammad, I am Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The noble Ibn Al-Karim Ibn Al-Karim Ibn Al-Karim Yusuf bin Yaqoub bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim Khalil Al-Rahman, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ If I had stayed in prison as long as Joseph had stayed, and then the supplicant came to me, I would have answered him, since: The Messenger came to him and said, “Go back to your Lord and ask Him what is the matter.” “The women who cut off their hands” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10741","I am Al-Hasan bin Muhammad, from Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ibn Abi Mulaika told me, Urwa told me, on the authority of Aisha, that she She disagreed with that and refused. She said: “God did not promise anything to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, except that He knew that it would happen until he died, and that He The calamities did not cease to befall the messengers until they thought that the believers who were with them had denied them.” Ibn Abi Mulaika said in the hadith of Urwah: And it was Aisha reads it: 0 They thought they had been lied to 0, burdened (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10742","I am Qutayba bin Saeed. Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Abi Mulaika informed me, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: “Until When the messengers became discouraged and thought that they had been lied to, he said: He went here, and pointed to the sky. Ibn Abi Mulaika said: And Ibn Abbas: Until the Messenger and those who believed with him say, “When is God’s victory?” Indeed, God’s victory is near. Ibn Abi Mulaika said: So I mentioned that. According to Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: Aisha said: “God forbid, by God, God Almighty never told His Messenger anything except that he knew that it would happen before That he would die, but calamity descended upon the prophets to the point that they feared that those who were with them among the believers had denied them, and it used to be read: 0 They were lied to. 0, burdened\ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"10743","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Wahb bin Jarir, narrated by my father, on the authority of Kulthum bin Jabr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that He read: “Even when the messengers despaired and thought that they had been lied to, only slightly. He said: Even when the messengers despaired of the faith of their people, and thought their people that the messengers have lied to them.”"
"10744","I am Ali bin Hajar, on the authority of Ismail, who is Ibn Jafar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “The keys to the unseen are five that no one knows except God: No one knows what the wombs close except God, no one knows what is tomorrow except God, and no one knows “No one knows when the rain will come except God, and no soul knows in what land it will die, and no one knows when the Hour will come except God Almighty.”"
"10745","I am Amr bin Mansour, this is Abdullah bin Abdul Wahhab, he said: Ali bin Abi Sarah narrated to me, Thabit Al-Bunani narrated to us, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, once sent a man to one of the Arab pharaohs to pray for me. He said: O Messenger of God, He is more powerful than that. He said: “Go to him and invite him.” He said: So he came to him and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is calling you. He said: Messenger God? What is God? Is it gold? Or is it silver? Is it from copper? So he returned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I told you that he is more powerful than that, and he told the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He acknowledged what he said. He said: “Go back to him and invite him.” He came back and repeated the first statement to him. He responded to him in the same manner as the answer, so he came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. So he told him, and he said: “Go back to him and invite him.” So he returned to him, and while they were discussing the conversation between them, he sent God was a cloud around his head, and it thundered and a thunderbolt fell from it and struck the skull of his head, and God Almighty sent down: And He sends the thunderbolts Then He afflicts with it whomever He wills, while they dispute about God, and He is severe in resistance.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10746","I am Muhammad bin Muslim. He said: Ismail bin Ubaid bin Abi Karimah narrated to me. He said: Muhammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahim, on the authority of Zayd bin Abi Anisa, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Abi Bin Ka’b, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And he said: “One day Moses stood up among his people and reminded them of the days of God, and the days of God are His blessings.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10747","I am Ali bin Hajar, I am Ismail, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, who The tree is a tree whose leaves do not fall, and it is like a believer, so tell me what it is.” Abdullah said: The people fell into the trees of the desert, and he fell. I thought to myself that it was the palm tree, so I was ashamed and they said: Tell us what it is, O Messenger of God? He said: “It is the palm tree.”"
"10748","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am An-Nadr bin Shumail, I am Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Shuaib bin Al-Hubhab, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: I came The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a veil of cover, recited: “And the likeness of a good word is like a good tree. He said: It is the palm tree.”"
"10749","I am Suwayd bin Nasr, I am Abdullah, on the authority of Safwan bin Amr, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Busr, on the authority of Abu Umamah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace in his saying: “And he will be given some purulent water to drink {16} and he will gulp it down. He said: Bring it near to him and he will reject it, so when he is brought a little closer to it, His face, and his scalp fell, so when he drank it, he cut his intestines until it came out of his anus. God Almighty says: And give them to drink hot water. So he cut their intestines, and God Almighty says: And if they cry for help, they will be helped with water like dead water, which scalds the faces. What a miserable drink. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10750","I am Muhammad bin Bashar, we are Muhammad, we are Shu’bah, on the authority of Alqamah bin Marthad, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: “God gives firmness to those who believe in the firm word in the life of this world. He said: It was sent down in the torment of the grave. It is said to him: Who is your Lord? Then he says: My Lord is God, and the Prophet of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. That is His saying: God establishes those who believe with the firm word in \the life of this world\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"10751","I am Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar, from Yahya bin Abi Bukayr, from us as a partner, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas in His saying: “God strengthens those who believe with the firm word in the life of this world. He said: Addressing people in the grave: Who is your Lord? What is your religion? And who is He? Your Prophet, and in the Hereafter, like that? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10752","I am Ishaq bin Mansour, I am Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Khaythamah, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib: “God strengthens those who “Believe in the word that is established regarding the life of this world. He said: It was sent down in the torment of the grave.”"
"10753","I am Muhammad bin Bashar, we are Muhammad, we are Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abi Bazza, on the authority of Abu Tufayl, he heard Ali, may God be pleased with him, and asked him Ibn Al-Kawwa’, on the authority of this verse: “Those who exchanged the blessings of God for disbelief and made their people dwell in an abode of destruction {28} Hell, they will dwell in it. He said: They were the infidels of Quraysh on the day of Badr. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10754","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the Almighty’s saying: “Have you not seen the Those who exchanged the blessings of God for disbelief and made their people an abode of destruction. He said: They are the people of Mecca. Sufyan said: He means their disbelievers."
"10755","I am Yunus bin Abdul-Ala, narrated by Ibn Wahb. Amr bin Al-Harith told me that Bakr bin Sawada told him, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Asi, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited the words of God Almighty regarding Abraham: “My Lord, they are They misled many people, the verse, and Jesus said: If you punish them, then they are your servants, and if you forgive them, then you are the Mighty, the Wise. So he raised his hands and said: Oh God, my nation, my nation, and he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, cried, and God said: O Gabriel, go to Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And your Lord knows best, so ask him what makes him cry. Then Gabriel came to him and asked him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told him what he said while he was there. I know, so God said: O Gabriel, go to Muhammad, and say to him: We will satisfy you among your nation, and there will be no worse than you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10756","I am Suwayd bin Nasr, I am Abdullah, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Salem bin Abdullah told me, on the authority of his father: that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace When he passed by the Hijr, peace be upon him, he said: “Do not enter the dwellings of those who have wronged themselves unless you are weeping, lest something like this befall you.” “It struck them.” He covered himself with his cloak while on the journey. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10757","Othman bin Abdullah told me, he said: Muhammad bin Abbad Al-Makki told me, Hatim bin Ismail told me, Abu Al-Hasan Al-Sayrifi told me, and he is Bassam, on the authority of Yazid bin Suhaib al-Faqir, who said: We were with Jabir, and he mentioned the Kharijites. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed People from my nation will be tortured for their sins, and they will be in Hell as long as God wills them to be. Then the polytheists will taunt them and say to them: What do we see? Whatever you used to differ from us about, such as your belief and your faith, has benefited you, because God wants to make the people of polytheism see regret, so what remains monotheistic Unless God takes him out.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited this verse: “Perhaps those who disbelieve wish they were Muslims.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10758","Kathir bin Ubaid told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Harb, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, that Abdullah bin Abbas, he said: A man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, from the Ansar, told me: While they were sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: Then a star was shot and it was illuminated. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What did you say in the pre-Islamic period when something like this was shot? They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: A great man was born tonight, and a great man died tonight. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. He said: “It is not thrown for the death of anyone, or for the life of someone, but rather when our Lord, Blessed and Most High, decrees a matter, those who bear the Throne glorify Him, then The inhabitants of heaven glorified those next to them, until the praise reached the inhabitants of this heaven. Then those next to the bearers of the throne said to the bearers of the throne: What did your Lord say? So they will inform them, and the inhabitants of heaven will inform one another until the news reaches this lowest heaven. Then the jinn snatch the hearing, and they throw it to their guardians, and they throw away what they brought on its face, for it is the truth, but they distort it. \And they increase\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"10759","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, from Nuh, who is Ibn Qais, on the authority of Ibn Malik, meaning Omar, on the authority of Abu al-Jawza, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “ There was a woman praying behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a beautiful woman from the best of people. He said: Some of the people were advancing in the first row. Because he does not see it, and some of them delay until they are in the back row, so if he kneels and mentions a word that means: he looked under his armpits, Then God Almighty revealed: “And We certainly knew those who came forward among you, and We certainly knew those who would come later.”"
"10760","I am Ali bin Hajar, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, that he heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: To the owners of the quarantine: “Do not enter upon these tormented people unless you are weeping. If you are not weeping, then do not enter upon them. “It will befall you like what befell them.”"
"10761","I am Muhammad bin Bashar, we are Yahya, we are Shu`bah, Khubayb bin Abdul Rahman narrated to me, on the authority of Hafs bin Asim, on the authority of Abu Saeed bin Al-Mu’alla. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by me while I was in the mosque, so he called me, but I did not come to him. He said: “What prevented you from coming to me?” I said: I did. I was praying. He said: “Didn’t God Almighty say: O you who have believed, respond to God and to the Messenger when he calls you for a reason that will revive you?” He said: “ Shall I not teach you the best surah in the Qur’an before I go out?” So when he went to go out, I mentioned that to him. He said: “Praise be to God, Lord.” of the worlds, they are the seven oft-repeated, and the Great Qur’an which I have been given.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10762","I am Ali bin Hajar, I am a partner, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, I am Ahmad bin Sulaiman, we are Ubaid Allah bin Musa, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in his saying: “And We have given you seven of the repeated Qur’an and the Great Qur’an.” He said: “The Al-Baqarah, and the Imran, the women, the customs, the livestock, and the table.” Sharik said: “The seven long ones.”"
"10763","I am Qutaybah bin Saeed, on the authority of Ya’qub, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Ba’ja bin Badr al-Juhani, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “The best life that people have ever known is a man who holds the reins of his horse in the path of God. Whenever he hears a sound or a fright, he flies on board. His horse and he sought death in his place, or as a man in one of these valleys, or in the depths of one of these valleys, in his spoils. He establishes prayer, pays zakat, and worships God until certainty comes to him. He is not among people except in the best.”"
"10764","I am Yahya bin Hakim, from Ibn Abi Adi, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ya’la bin Ata, on the authority of Waki’ bin Adas, on the authority of his uncle Abi Razin. Al-Uqaili said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The likeness of a believer is like a bee. It does not eat anything but good things, and it does not put away anything except good things.”"
"10765","We are Al-Hussein bin Harith, I am Al-Fadl bin Musa, on the authority of Issa bin Ubaid, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Abi Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Abi bin Ka’b, he said: When On the day of Uhud, sixty-four Ansar men were injured, and six of the Muhajireen were injured, including Hamza. They mutilated him, and the Ansar said: If a day like this befalls us from them, we will certainly raise against them. And when it was the day of the conquest of Mecca, God Almighty revealed: Whatever you punish, punish with the same way you were punished, and if you are patient, it is better for those who are patient. Then a man said, “There will be no Quraysh after today.” So the Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Keep away from the people, except four.”"
"10766","I am Muhammad bin Bashar, from Yahya, he said: from Sufyan, he said: Asim told me, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: “Glory be to Him who took captives.” of His servant at night from the Sacred Mosque to the Al-Aqsa Mosque. He said: He did not pray in it, and if he had prayed in it, it would have been prescribed for you, just as it was prescribed for you to pray in The Kaaba (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10767","I am Ali bin Hajar, narrated to me Ali bin Mushar, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: I used to recite the Qur’an to my father on the path, so when I recited... Prostration He prostrated, I said to him: Father, do you prostrate on the road? He said: I heard Abu Dharr say: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the first mosque placed on earth, and he said: “The mosque.” The forbidden.” I said: Then what? He said: “Al-Aqsa Mosque.” I said: How much is there between them? He said: “Forty years, and the earth is a mosque for you, so wherever you reach prayer, pray.”"
"10768","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Jabir: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said “When the Quraysh denied me, I stood up in Al-Hijr, and God revealed to me the Holy House, and I began to tell them about His signs as I looked at it.”"
"10769","I am Abu Dawud Suleiman bin Saif, he said: I am Abu al-Numan, I am Thabit, he said: I am Hilal, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “He was captured.” of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to the Holy House, then he came that night and told them about his journey and the sign of the Holy House and their camel. Then some people said: We do not believe Muhammad, so they turned into infidels, so God struck their necks along with Abu Jahl.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10770","I am Muhammad bin Rafi’, on the authority of Hujain bin Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Abdul Aziz, and he is Al-Majishun, on the authority of Ibn Al-Fadl, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You saw me in Al-Hijr, and the Quraysh were asking me about my journey, so they asked me about things from... I did not go to the Holy House, and I was in distress such as I had never experienced before, so God Almighty raised it up for me to look at, and they did not ask me about anything except I brought it to them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10771","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us in his hadith, on the authority of Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman, he said: I heard Awf, on the authority of Zurara, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “On the night I was taken on a captivity, and then in the morning in Mecca, he said: I have cut off my affairs and I know that the people are my liars.” He said: So I sat isolated and sad, then the enemy of God, Abu Jahl, passed by me, and he came until he sat next to him, and he said to him like a mocker: Was there anything? He said: “Yes.” He said: What is it? He said: “I will be taken on a journey tonight.” He said: Where? He said: “To the Holy House.” He said: Then you were among us in the morning? He said: “Yes.” He said: He did not see that he was telling him a liar for fear that he would deny the hadith if he called his people for him. He said: If I call your people to you Do you talk to them? He said: “Yes.” Abu Jahl said: The people of Banu Ka’b bin Luayy, come. Then the gatherings broke up and they came and sat down to them. He said: Tell your people what you told me. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I will be taken on the journey tonight.” They said: Where to? He said: “To the Holy House.” He said: They said: Then you spent the morning among us? He said: “Yes.” Among the people who believed him, and among those who put his hand on his head and marveled at lying, said: And among the people is he who travels to that. The country, and he saw the mosque. He said: They said: Can you grant us the mosque? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “So I went and addressed them, and I continued to describe them until some of the epithet became confused for me.” He said: “Then he came.” “In the mosque until it was established.” He said: “So I called the mosque while I was looking at it.” He said: There was a hadith with this that I forgot as well. He said The people: As for the epithet, it is correct (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10772","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us — Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us — Abu Hayyan narrated to me — Abu Zur'a ibn 'Amr ibn Jarir narrated to me, from Abu Huraira, who said: \The Messenger of Allah"
"10773","I am Muhammad bin Mansour, from Sufyan, from Sulayman, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “There was a group of people They worshiped the jinn, so the jinn submitted to Islam and mankind remained steadfast in their worship, so God Almighty revealed: Those whom they call upon seek to Their Lord is the means.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10774","I am Muhammad Ibn Al-Ala, I am Ibn Idris, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Abdullah: “Those are those who call upon They seek the means to their Lord. He said: A group of mankind used to worship a group of jinn, so they converted to Islam, and those who worshiped them remained. On their worship, and he said: Those are those whom they call upon, seeking a way to their Lord. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10775","I am Amr bin Ali, from Yahya, he said: from Sufyan, Sulayman said: on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Abdullah, in his saying: Those are those whom they call upon, seeking a way to their Lord. He said: Some people from among humanity were worshiping people from among the jinn, so the jinn submitted and held on to Islam. These are their religion.”"
"10776","I am Zakaria bin Yahya, from Ishaq, from Jarir, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ja’far bin Iyas, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The people of Mecca asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to make for them Al-Safa gold, and to remove the mountains from them so that they might be planted. He said God Almighty: If You wish, We will give them what they asked. If they disbelieve, they will be destroyed as those before them were destroyed. And if You wish, We may seek privacy with them. Perhaps we may Let us extract from them, and he said: No, rather I seek refuge with them. Then God revealed this verse: And nothing prevented Us from sending signs unless he denied them. And We gave Thamud the she-camel sighted."
"10777","I am Muhammad Ibn Al-Ala, I am Ibn Idris, I am Al-Hasan Ibn Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in: “And We did not create the vision which We showed you. He said: When he was taken on the journey. He said: And the tree cursed in the Qur’an. He said: It is the tree of Zaqqum. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10778","10789 Muhammad bin Mansour, narrated by Sufyan, informed us on the authority of Amr, who heard Ikrimah speaking, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in his saying: “ And the tree cursed in the Qur’an. He said: It is the tree of Zaqqum: And We did not make the vision that we showed you. He said: A vision with an eye that the Prophet saw, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, the night he was taken captive.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10779","I am Ubaid bin Asbat bin Muhammad, from my father, from Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in his saying “And the Fajr Qur’an is witnessed. He said: The angels of the night and the angels of the day witness it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10780","I am Ismail bin Masoud, he said: Khaled told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he heard him say: I heard Silah bin Zufar, saying: I heard Hudhayfah says: “The people will gather in a plain, and not a single soul will speak. The first person to be invited will be Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he will say: ‘Labbayk wa Asa’idika’. Good is in your hands, and evil is not from you, and the Mahdi is whom you have guided, and your servant and the son of your servant, and through you and to you, and there is no refuge or refuge from you. Except to You, Blessed and Exalted are You. This is what He says: Perhaps your Lord will raise you to a praiseworthy station.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10781","I am Al-Abbas bin Abdullah bin Al-Abbas, he said: Saeed bin Mansour Al-Makki told us, Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Adam bin Ali, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “On the Day of Resurrection, people will become corpses. Every nation will follow its prophet. They say: Yes, so-and-so, intercede for us, until intercession goes to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. That is the day when God, Blessed and Exalted, will resurrect him. And exalted be He the Praiseworthy Station.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10782","I am Muhammad bin Bashar, we are Muhammad bin Jaafar, we are Shu’bah, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, he said: I heard Abu al-Za’ra’, he said: On the authority of Abdullah, in A story he mentioned: “The first intercessor on the Day of Resurrection will be Gabriel, peace be upon him, the Holy Spirit, then Abraham, the friend of the Most Gracious, peace be upon him, then Moses, or Jesus.” Abu al-Za’ra’ said: I do not know which one he said. He said: “Then your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, will rise a fourth time, and no one will intercede.” The like of His intercession, and it is His praiseworthy promise that He promised.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10783","I am Ubayd Allah bin Saeed, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God entered May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he entered Mecca, and around the House were three hundred and sixty idols. He started stabbing a stick in his hand and saying: “The truth has come and has vanished.” Falsehood. Indeed, falsehood was vanishing, and the truth has come. And what initiates falsehood, nor does it bring it back.”"
"10784","I am Ahmad ibn Sulayman, narrated to us Zayn ibn al-Hubab, narrated to us Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah, and narrated to me Salam ibn Miskin ibn Rabiah al-Namari, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abdullah ibn Rabah al-Ansari, who said: We came as a delegation to Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, and Abu Hurayrah was with us, and that was in the month of Ramadan. Abu Hurayrah frequently invited people to his camp, so I said to my family: Prepare some food for us, and they did so. I met Abu Hurayrah in the late afternoon and said: The invitation is at my place tonight. He said: You have preceded me to it. I said: Yes. So he came to us and said: O company of the Ansar, shall I not inform you of a hadith from your hadith? He said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, conquered Makkah, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, appointed al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam over one of the two flanks, and Khalid ibn al-Walid over the other. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, spotted me in a crowd and called out to me. I said: Here I am, O Messenger of Allah. He said: \Call out to the Ansar for me.\"" So I called out to them"
"10785","I am Ali bin Khashram, I am Isa, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: I was walking with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted a man in Harith in Medina while leaning on Asib. He passed by a group of Jews, and some of them said: If you ask him, and some of them said: No. You ask him and he makes you hear what you dislike. So they stood up to him and said: O Abu al-Qasim, tell us about the soul. So he stood up for an hour and raised his head. So we knew that it was being revealed to him, until the revelation came, then he said: “The spirit is from the command of my Lord, and you have not been given of knowledge except a little.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10786","On the authority of Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Bukair, on the authority of Shibl bin Abbad, on the authority of Abu Qaza Suwayd bin Hujayr, On the authority of Hakim ibn Muawiyah, on the authority of his father Muawiyah ibn Hudaydah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “You will gather men and riders.” And you will be dragged on your faces.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10787","Ya'qub bin Ibrahim, narrated to us by Hushaym, I am Abu Bishr, informed us on the authority of Sa'id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the words of the Almighty: And do not recite your prayer loudly, and do not recite it silently. He said: It was revealed while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was hidden in Mecca. Whenever he prayed with his companions He raised his voice while reciting, so when the polytheists heard it, they cursed the Qur’an, and whoever sent it down, and whoever brought it, and he said to his Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him: And do not recite your prayers out loud, that is, with your recitation, lest the polytheists hear and curse the Qur’an, and do not frighten your companions with it, lest they listen. And seek a way between that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10788","I am Harun bin Ishaq, descended from Abda, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father. And I am Shuaib bin Yusuf. He said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Aisha, in the words of the Almighty: And do not recite your prayer out loud, and do not recite it silently, it was revealed in supplication.”"
"10789","I am Ibrahim bin Muhammad, from Ibn Dawud, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Suleiman bin Dawud, peace be upon them, said: I will go around a hundred women tonight, and each woman will bring a man.” He struck with a sword, but he did not say: If God wills, so he went around them and one of them brought with half an offspring. If Solomon had said: If God wills, it would not have happened. \He said\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"10790","I am Abu Salih al-Makki, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of al-A’mash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Abu Dharr: That the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he greeted him. He said to him: “O Abu Dharr, shall I not direct you to one of the treasures of Paradise?” He said: Yes. He said: It says: There is no power nor strength except in God. \""
10791"""
"10791","Muhammad ibn 'Abdul-A'la (said): Khalid narrated to us, (saying): Hatim narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah, who said: Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrated to me, that 'A'ishah said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""You will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised (ghurlan)."" 'A'ishah said: I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, the men and the women looking at one another?"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The matter is more severe than that they should be concerned with that."""
"10792","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, that Hussein bin Ali narrated to him, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, said that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to him and Fatima, may God be pleased with them, and said: “Aren’t you praying?” I said: O Messenger. By God, our lives are in the hands of God. If He wishes to send them away, He sends them. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, departed while he was heading back. He hits his thigh and says: “And man was the most argumentative.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10793","I am Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamir, narrated to us al-Salt ibn Muhammad, narrated to us Maslamah ibn Alqamah, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: \Musa stood as an address among the Children of Israel and delivered an eloquent sermon. It occurred to him that no one had been given the knowledge that he had been given. Allah knew what he had whispered to himself concerning that. He said to him: O Musa"
"10794","I am Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala, narrated to us al-Mutamir, from his father, from Raqabah, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Jubayr, who said: It was said to Ibn Abbas: Indeed Nawf claims that Musa, peace be upon him, who went seeking knowledge is not Musa of the Children of Israel. He said: Did you hear that, O Said? He said: Yes. He said: Nawf has lied. Ubayy ibn Kab narrated to us, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: \While Musa"
"10795","I am Qutaybah ibn Said, in his hadith, from Sufyan, from Amr, from Said ibn Jubayr, who said: I said to Ibn Abbas: Indeed Nawf al-Bakali claims that Musa of the Children of Israel is not the Musa of al-Khadir. He said: The enemy of Allah has lied. Ubayy ibn Kab narrated to us, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: \Musa"
"10796","Imran bin Yazid informed me, narrated to me Ismail bin Abdullah bin Sama’ah, on the authority of Al-Awza’i. He said: Ibn Shihab informed me, on the authority of Ubaid. Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he and Al-Hurr bin Qais bin Hisn Al-Fazari disputed over Musa’s companion, he said Ibn Abbas: He is Khidr. Ubayy ibn Ka’b al-Ansari passed by them, and Ibn Abbas called him and said: I have been plotting, and this companion of mine is in the midst of a companion. Moses, who asked the way to meet him, did you hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mention something? He said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “While Moses was in the presence of a group of the Children of Israel, when a man came to him and said: Did Do you know anyone more knowledgeable than you? Then Moses, peace be upon him, said: No. So God revealed to Moses: Yes, our servant Khidr. So Moses, peace be upon him, asked the way to meet him. So God made the whale a sign for him, and it was said: If you miss the whale, return, for you will meet it. Moses, peace be upon him, was following the trail of the whale in the sea. Moses' boy said to Moses: Did you see that when we took refuge on the rock, I forgot the fish, and no one but Satan made me forget to mention it? Moses said Peace be upon him: That is what we wanted, so they returned stories in their tracks, and they found greenness, so it was their business what God related in His Book."
"10797","I am Muhammad bin Ali bin Maimun, from Al-Faryabi, from Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of my father Ibn Ka’b, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in his saying: “They refused to give them hospitality. He said: They were mean people of a town.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10798","Muhammad ibn al-Khalil informed us, on the authority of Hajjaj ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Hamza al-Zayat, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned someone, he would supplicate for him, he would start with himself, and he would say the same thing. A day: “May God’s mercy be upon us and upon Moses. If he had stayed with his companion, he would have seen the astonishment, but he said: If I ask you about anything after that, do not Accompany me, for you have attained an excuse from me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10799","I am Ubayd Allah bin Saeed, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, I heard him say: On the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Zainab, on the authority of Habiba, on the authority of her mother, Umm Habiba, on the authority of Zainab bint Jahsh, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, woke up from sleep, his face red, and he said: “There is no god.” Except Allah, three times. Woe to the Arabs because of the evil that has approached. Today is opened from the back of Dam, Gog, and Magog like this, and seventy years ago. And ten all the same. I said: O Messenger of God, will we perish while among us are the righteous? He said: Yes, if evil abounds?"
"10800","I am Amr bin Zurarah. He said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Aslam al-Ijli, on the authority of Bishr bin Shaghaf, on the authority of Abdullah Bin Amr, he said: A Bedouin said: O Messenger of God, what are the pictures? He said: “A horn that is blown into.”"
"10801","I am Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim, from Yazid, from Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Sa’d, who said: A man asked my father about This verse: “Say: Shall we inform you of the deeds of those who will lose, the most important of whom is the Hurriyah?” He said: No, they are the People of the Book. As for the Jews, they disbelieved in Muhammad. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. As for the Christians, they disbelieved in Paradise. They said: There is neither food nor drink, but it is the Hurriyah whom God Almighty said: And they cut off what God has commanded to be joined, and they spread corruption in the land, to: the transgressors.” Yazid said: “This is how I have preserved,” and Sa’d used to name them. The sinners (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10802","Narrated by Qutayba bin Saeed, narrated by Yahya bin Zakaria bin Abi Zaida, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “She said Quraysh told the Jews: Give us something with which to ask this man. They said: Ask him about the soul. So they asked him, and it was revealed: And they ask you about the soul. Say The spirit is from the command of my Lord, and you have not been given of knowledge except a little. They said: We have been given much knowledge, we have been given the Torah, and whoever has been given the Torah has been given good. So much, so God revealed: “Say, ‘If the sea were ink for the words of my Lord, the sea would be exhausted.’”"
"10803","I am Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Ayyub, ibn Idris, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Alqamah ibn Wa’il, on the authority of Al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I was in the land of Najran and they asked me, and they said: Did you see something that you read: O sister of Aaron, between Moses and Jesus that had Have you known for years? He said: I did not know what to answer them with, so when I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I mentioned that to him, and he said: “Didn’t you tell them?” “They were called by their prophets and the righteous.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10804","I am Hanad bin Al-Sirri, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Saeed, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If The people of Hell will enter Hell, and the people of Paradise will enter Paradise. Death will be brought as if it were a salty ram, and a herald will call: O people of Paradise! Do you know this? He said: Then they drink and look, and everyone has seen it, and they say: Yes, this is death. Then he will call: O people of Hell Do you know this? So they drink and look, and they all have seen it, and they say: Yes, this is death, and they are taken and slaughtered, then He will call out: O people of Paradise, eternity and death, and O people of Hell, eternity and death. That is His saying: And warn them of the Day of Regret when The matter was decided while they were heedless. He said: The people of this world are heedless. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10805","I am Muhammad bin Ubaid bin Muhammad, from Asbat, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in This verse: “And warn them of the Day of Regret.” He said: He will call: O people of Paradise, and they will drink and look on. And He will call: O people of Hell. So they drink and look, and it is said: Do you know death? They say: Yes, then death comes in the form of a salty ram, and it is said: This is death. It is presented and slaughtered. He said: O people of Paradise, eternity, not death. And it is said: O people of Hell, eternity, not death. He said: Then he recited: And warn them of the Day of Regret when the matter has been decided.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10806","I am Ubaidullah bin Fadalah bin Ibrahim, I am Musa bin Ismail, I am Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Jundub, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Adam met Moses, and Moses said: O Adam, you are the one whom God created with His hand, and to whom His angels prostrated. And He made you dwell in His Paradise, and breathed into you of His Spirit. Adam said: O Moses, you are the one whom God chose with His messages, and gave you the Torah, and spoke to you. And He brought you near in salvation, so should I come first or the male? The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: So Adam performed Hajj, Moses, so Adam performed Hajj, Moses. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10807","I am Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Amer, he said: Omar told us, he said: My father told us. And I am Ibrahim bin Al-Hassan, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Muhammad, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said Muhammad: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and Abraham said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Gabriel: “What prevents you from visiting us?” “And we do not come down except by the command of your Lord.” Muhammad said: The verse. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10808","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: “No one who dies and has three children enters the Fire, unless the oath is dissolved.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10809","I am Al-Hasan bin Muhammad, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj. And Harun bin Abdullah, Na Hajjaj, told me. Ibn Jurayj said: Abu Al-Zubayr told me, that he heard Jabir, saying: You told me Umm Mubashir said that she heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying, in the presence of Hafsa, may God be pleased with her: “No one of the companions of God will enter Hell, God willing.” The tree is one of those who pledged allegiance under it. She said: Yes, O Messenger of God. So he rebuked her. Hafsa said: And there is not one of you except him who will enter it. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God has said: Then We will save those who feared, and We will leave the wrongdoers therein kneeling.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10810","I am Muhammad bin Al-Ala, from Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Khabab, who said: “I was a firm man, and I had Al-Asi bin Wael owed a debt, so I went to him to pay it, and he said: By God, I will not pay you off until you disbelieve in Muhammad. So I said: No, by God, I will not disbelieve in Muhammad until you disbelieve. You die and then are resurrected. He said: If I die and are resurrected, you will come to me as my guardian, then wealth and a child, and I will give you. Then God Almighty revealed: Have you seen? He who disbelieves in Our signs until he says: And He will come to Us alone.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10811","I am Hanad bin Al-Sari, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No one is more patient than the harm he hears from God. And He provides for them, and protects them from them.”"
"10812","I am Ismail bin Masoud, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ibn Hazan, who said: The people of camels and sheep were proud, Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Moses, peace be upon him, was sent and he was a shepherd, and David, peace be upon him, was sent and he was a sheep shepherd. “And I was sent to tend sheep for my family with my family in Ajyad.”"
"10813","I am Abdullah ibn Muhammad, narrated to us Yazid ibn Harun, narrated to us Asbag ibn Zayd, narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Abi Ayyub, narrated to me Said ibn Jubayr, who said: I asked Abdullah ibn Abbas about the words of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, to Musa, peace be upon him: 'And We tried you with trials' (Quran 20:40). I asked him about the trials—what are they? He said: Begin the day anew, O Ibn Jubayr, for it has a long narrative. When I woke up, I went to Ibn Abbas to claim from him what he had promised me regarding the hadith of the trials. He said: \Pharaoh and his courtiers discussed what Allah"
"10814","I am Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, I am Khaled, I am Uthman, that Abu Nadhrah narrated to them, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri: that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The people will be gathered at the bridge of Hell, and there will be thorns and thorns over it, and the people will pass by. He said: Then it will pass by them like lightning. And some of them are like a galloping horse, and some of them run, and some of them walk, and some of them crawl, and dogs catch them, And the angels by his sides said: O God, grant us peace, grant us peace, and the dogs will snatch them away. He said: “As for its people, who are its people, they will not die.” And they will not live, but as for some people who are taken for trespasses and sins, they will be burned and become charcoal. On a river from Paradise, and they will grow just as a seed grows in the depths of a torrent.” He said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Have you seen the dyed ones? After they are given permission and they enter Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10815","I am Amr bin Mansour, we are Al-Hasan bin Al-Rabi’, we are Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Abu Laila, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us with a blind man in his hand, and he said: “This is from manna.” And its water is a cure for the eyes.”"
"10816","I am Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid, from Ayyub bin Al-Najjar, the Hanafi al-Yamimi, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me, on the authority of Abu Salamah Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Adam argued with Moses, and he said to him: O Adam, you are the one who You took people out of Paradise and made them miserable. Adam said: O Moses, you are the one whom God chose with His message and His words. Do you blame me for something? Did God prescribe it for me, or decreed it for me, before He created me? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “So Adam and Moses performed Hajj.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10817","I am Yaqoub bin Ibrahim, narrated by Abdullah bin Idris, who said: I heard Ismail bin Abi Khaled mentioning, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Jarir bin Abdullah, he said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he looked at the moon on the night of the full moon, and he said: “You will see Your Lord, as you see this, you will not be troubled by seeing it, for if you are able not to neglect a prayer before sunrise and before its setting So do so. Then he recited: “And glorify the praises of your Lord before the sun rises and before it sets.”"
"10818","I am Ziyad bin Ayyub, from Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Saeed, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: And they were heedless. He said: In this world. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10819","I am Ahmad bin Nasr, I am Hisham bin Abdul Malik Abu Al-Walid Al-Tayalisi, we are Abu Muawiyah, we are Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Saeed, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “In heedlessness, we turn away.” He said: “In this world.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10820","I am Ubayd Allah bin Ibrahim, from my uncle, from my father, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Urwa bin Al-Zubayr told me that Zainab is the daughter of my father Salamah reported, on the authority of Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan, on the authority of Zainab bint Jahsh, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon her in fear, saying: “There is no god but God. Woe to the Arabs, from the evil that has approached. Today, Gog and Magog have been opened from the ruins of Gog and Magog like this.” He said: And he flew. With his thumb and the next, I said: O Messenger of God, shall we perish while among us are the righteous? He said: “Yes, if the wickedness is great.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10821","I am Abu Dawud, from Sahl bin Hammad, from Shu`bah, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Salem, on the authority of Ibn Amr bin Aws, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, Gog and Magog have women with whom they may have intercourse with whomever they wish, and trees with which they may pollinate whomever they wish. Not one of them dies but leaves behind a thousand of his descendants and more.”"
"10822","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Nuh, on the authority of Yazid bin Ka’b, on the authority of Amr bin Malik, on the authority of Abu Al-Jawza, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “ The record: the scribe of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10823","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Nuh, on the authority of Amr bin Malik, on the authority of Abu Al-Jawza, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he used to say in this verse: “ On the day We fold up the sky like the folding of a log, he said: The log is the man.”"
"10824","I am Suleiman bin Ubayd Allah bin Amr, I am Bahz, I am Shu`bah, I am Al-Mughirah bin Al-Numan. He said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr speaking, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up to deliver a sermon, and said: “O people, you will be gathered to your Lord, disheveled.” Uncircumcised, then he recited this verse: Just as We initiated the first creation, We will return him, until the end of the verse, and the first of the creation to be clothed was Abraham. Peace, and indeed, some people from my nation will be brought and taken to the north, so I will say: Lord of my companions, and He will say: You do not know what they did after you. So I say like what the righteous servant said: If you punish them, they are your servants, and if you forgive them, then you are the Mighty, the Wise. It is said: They have not continued to be apostates ever since I left them.”"
"10825","I am Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Shuaib bin Al-Layth, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God Almighty said: The son of Adam lied to me, and it was not appropriate for him to tell me a lie, and the son of Adam insulted me. Adam, and it was not appropriate for him to insult Me. As for his denial of Me, he said: I will not repeat it as I began it, and the last of creation is not more dear to Me than The beginning of it, and as for his cursing of me, he said: God has taken a son, and I am God, one of the eternal, I did not give birth, nor was I born, and there is no one equal to me.”"
"10826","I am Muhammad bin Al-Ala, I am Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ God, Blessed and Almighty, will say to Adam on the Day of Resurrection: O Adam, arise and send from your descendants the source of the Fire. Then He will say: O Lord, and what is the source of the Fire? So he says: From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine, and one is left. At that time, the little one will turn gray, and every pregnant female will give birth. He carried it and you see the people drunk, but they are not drunk, but the punishment of God is severe.” That was difficult for his companions, so they said: O Messenger of God, from all One thousand nine hundred and ninety-nine and there is one left, so which one is that one? So he entered his house and then went out to them and said: “From Gog and Magog are a thousand and from you is one, and rejoice, for I hope that you will be a quarter.” People of Paradise.” So they said “Allahu Akbar” and thanked God. He said: “I hope that you will be a third of the people of Paradise.” So they said “Allahu Akbar” and thanked God. He said: “I am I hope to God that you will be half the people of Paradise.” So they said “Allahu Akbar” and thanked God. He said: “Among the nations, you are nothing but like the white hair of a bull.” Black, or like the black hair on a white bull.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10827","I am Muhammad bin Bashar, from Yahya, from Hisham, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, he said: We were with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said the salutation while walking, and he dispersed among his companions as they walked, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, raised his voice with these two verses: “O people! Fear your Lord. Indeed, the earthquake of the Hour is a great thing. {1} On the day when you will see it, every nursing woman will be astonished at what she has breastfed, and every pregnant female will give birth to her burden. And you see people drunk, but they are not drunk, but the punishment of God is severe. {2} So when his companions heard of that, they knew that it was something he was saying, so he said: Do you know what day that is? They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: That is a day on which God will call: O Adam, send forth a resurrection of the Fire. He will say: O Lord, and what is the resurrection of the Fire? He says: “Out of every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine will be in Hell, and one will be in Paradise.” So he made the people foolish to the point that they explained it with a laugh. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw those with his companions, he said: “Work and give good tidings. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, you are a shining light.” Two creatures who were not with anything but multiplied it: Gog and Magog, and whoever of the sons of Adam who died, and the sons of Satan.” He said: So he was secreted from the people. Some of those who found it, so he said: “Work and give good news. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, you are among the people no more than a mole on the side of a camel, or Like a lump in the arm of an animal.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10828","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Qays ibn Abbad, he said: I heard Abu Dharr swears: This verse was revealed: “These are two adversaries who disputed about their Lord, concerning: Ali, Hamza, and Ubaid bin Al-Harith. Shaybah bin Rabi’ah, Utbah bin Rabi’ah, and Al-Walid bin Utbah quarreled on the day of Badr.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10829","I am Hilal bin Bishr, we are Yusuf bin Yaqoub, we are Sulayman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Qais bin Abbad, on the authority of Ali, peace be upon him, he said: “ This verse was revealed about us, during our duel on the day of Badr: “These are two adversaries who disputed about their Lord.”"
"10830","I am Mahmoud bin Ghaylan, we are Al-Nadr bin Shumail, I am Shu’bah, we are Khalifa. He said: I heard Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr giving a sermon, and he said: No. Wear silk, for I heard Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever wears it in This world and he does not wear it in the Hereafter.” And Ibn al-Zubayr said: Whoever wears it in this world will not enter Paradise. God Almighty said: And their clothing It contains silk"
"10831","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, narrated by Hammad, on the authority of Thabit, who said: I heard Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, while he was on the pulpit delivering a sermon, saying: Muhammad said, May God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10832","I am Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam, I am Ishaq Al-Azraq, I am Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, left Mecca. Abu Bakr said: They expelled their Prophet. To Allah we belong and to Him we shall return.” We will certainly destroy them.’ Then it was revealed: Permission is given to those who fight because they have been wronged and that God is Able to grant them victory. So I knew that there would be a fight,” he said. Ibn Abbas said: It is the first verse revealed regarding fighting. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10833","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, narrated to me Muhammad bin Yahya, narrated to me Muhammad bin Abd al-Aziz bin Abi Rizmah, narrated to me Salmuwayh Abu Saleh, I Abdullah, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: It was the first verse revealed regarding fighting, as Urwah told me, on the authority of Aisha: “Give permission to those who They are fighting because they have been wronged, and indeed, God is Powerful to grant them victory, to His saying: Indeed, God is Powerful, Mighty. Then He gave permission for fighting in many verses. From the Qur’an” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10834","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, narrated by Al-Layth, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “The best you have ever ridden.” To Him are the departed people, this mosque of mine and the ancient House.”"
"10835","I am Muhammad bin Mansour, we are Al-Aswad bin Amer, I am Al-Thawri, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The poor Muslims will enter Paradise five hundred years before the rich, which is the equivalent of half a day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10836","I am Hisham bin Ammar, we are Muhammad bin Shuaib, Muawiyah bin Salam informed me that his brother Zayd bin Salam informed him, on the authority of Abu Salam, that He told him, he said: Al-Harith Al-Ash’ari informed me, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever calls according to the call of pre-Islamic times, then he From the knees of Hell.” A man said: O Messenger of God, and if he fasts and prays? He said: “Yes, and if he fasts and prays, then pray the supplication of God with which God has named you Muslims, believers, servants of God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10837","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, narrated by Jaafar, on the authority of Abu Imran, narrated by Yazid bin Babnus, who said: We said to Aisha: O Mother of the Believers, how was his creation? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? She said: “The creation of the Messenger of God was the Qur’an,” so she recited: The believers have succeeded, until she concluded: And those who are careful in their prayers, She said: This is how the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was created."
"10838","I am Ahmad bin Suleiman, narrated by Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, that he heard Saeed bin Jubayr speaking, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said “Indeed, the Samar hated it until this verse was revealed: ‘You are arrogant because of it. Samar is deserting you.’ He said: ‘They are arrogant in the House, saying: We are its people.’” Samar, he said: They were arrogant and were arrogant in it, but they did not inhabit it, they abandoned it."
"10839","I am Muhammad bin Aqeel, I am Ali bin Al-Hussein, narrated by my father, narrated by Yazid, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “Abu Sufyan came to the Prophet and prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Muhammad, I adjure you by God and the Most Merciful, for we have eaten dung, meaning lint and blood, so God Almighty revealed: “And We seized them with torment, but they did not submit to their Lord, nor did they supplicate.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10840","I am Muhammad bin Jafar bin Muhammad, we are Ali bin Al-Madini, we are Bashar bin Issa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, he said: Musa bin Uqba, he said: I heard Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in his saying: “With torment when they dare. {64} Do not dare today. Indeed, you You will not be helped from us. {65} He said: They are the people of Badr. Hamza bin Muhammad said: Muhammad bin Ja`far bin Imam told us: Ali bin told me. Al-Madini, with a similar chain of transmission. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10841","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, narrated by Al-Layth, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: When Khaybar was conquered, it was given to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. A sheep had poison in it, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Gather for me the Jews who were here.” So they gathered for him. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them: “I am asking you about something. Will you tell the truth about it?” They said: Yes, Abu al-Qasim. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to them: “Who is your father?” They said: So-and-so. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “You lied. “Your father is so-and-so.” They said: “You told the truth and you made justifications.” He said: “Would you tell the truth about something if I asked you about it?” They said: Yes, even if we lied You knew that we lied just as you knew about our father. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them: “Who are the people of Hell?” They said: We will be in it for a short time. Then you will leave us behind in it. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to them: “Be humble in it, and by God, we will never differ from you in it...”, and the hadith continued."
"10842","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, narrated by Al-Layth, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and Zaid bin Khalid, that they said: A man of the Bedouins came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I implore you to decree for me in writing. God, so the other opponent, who was more knowledgeable than him, said: Yes, and judge between us according to the Book of God, and give me permission, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said “Say,” and he said: “My son was stubborn about this, so he committed adultery with his wife, and I was informed that my son should be stoned, so I ransomed him with a hundred sheep.” With Walidah, I asked the people of knowledge, and they told me that my son should be subjected to one hundred lashes and a year of exile, and that the woman should be subjected to stoning. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I will decide between you according to the Book of God. The female child and the sheep shall be restored, and your son shall have One hundred lashes and exile for a year. Go, O Unays, to this woman and stone her.” So he went to her and she confessed, so he ordered her to be stoned."
"10843","I am Sawwar bin Abdullah bin Sawwar, we are Khaled bin Al-Harith, we are Abdul-Malik bin Abi Suleiman, Saeed bin Jubayr told me, he said: I came Ibn Omar, so I said: O Abu Abdul Rahman, should the two cursed people be separated? He said: Glory be to God. The first person to ask about that was so-and-so, and he said: O Messenger of God, a man sees his wife committing indecency, so if he speaks He spoke about a great matter, and if he remained silent, he remained silent about a great matter? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, remained silent about him. He came to him after that and said: O Messenger of God, you have been afflicted with the matter I asked you about. ? He said: “For God said: And those who accuse their wives and have no witnesses except themselves, the testimony of one of them is four testimonies.” By God, until he recited all the verses.” Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, reminded him and told him that the torment of this world is lesser than the torment of the Hereafter. He said: By the One who sent you with the truth, it is for the truth. Then he called the woman, and God reminded her and told her that the torment of this world is easier than The torment of the Hereafter, and she said: By the One who sent you with the truth, this was not the case. He said to the man: “Testify: Four testimonies of God. Indeed, he is one of The truthful {6} And the fifth is that the curse of God is upon him if he is of the liars {7} “Then the woman bore four testimonies that God For among the liars, and fifthly, that God’s wrath be upon her if he were of the truthful ones, then He separated between them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10844","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Jarir, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Sulaiman, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, he said: We asked Ibn Umar: Is there a difference between The cursed ones? He said: Glory be to God. Yes, a man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, have you seen one of us seeing his wife? Obscene, how is it done? So he remained silent about him and he did not answer him. Then he came to him and said: I have been afflicted with this, O Messenger of God. So God revealed these verses from Surat An-Nur, and he called. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the man testified four times that he is one of the truthful, and the fifth is that the curse of God is upon him if He was one of the liars. Then he made a mistake with the woman and she testified four times that God was one of the liars, and the fifth was that God was angry. upon her if he was one of the truthful ones. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, separated between them.”"
"10845","I am Amr bin Ali, we are Al-Mu`tamir bin Sulaiman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hadrami, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said “There was a woman called Umm Mahzul, and she was riding horses and was playing with horses. A man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to He marries her, so God Almighty revealed: And no one may marry an adulteress except an adulterer or a polytheist, and that is forbidden to the believers. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10846","I am Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā, narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Thawr, from Maʿmar, from Muḥammad ibn Muslim ibn Shihāb al-Zuhrī, who said: ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, ʿAlqama ibn Waqqāṣ, and ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah informed me of the ḥadīth of ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, when the people of the Slander said what they said about her, and Allāh declared her innocent. Each of them narrated to me a portion of her ḥadīth, and some of them were more retentive of her ḥadīth than others and more accurate in its transmission. I retained from each one of them the ḥadīth which he narrated to me, and some of their narrations corroborate others. They asserted that ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said:\n\n\The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ"
"10847","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman narrated to us, Abdullah bin Wahb narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Thawr bin Zayd, on the authority of Abu Al-Ghaith, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Avoid the seven calamities.” It was said: O Messenger of God, and what are they? He said: “Associating others with God, witchcraft, killing a soul that God has forbidden except in a just way, consuming usury, consuming an orphan’s property, and turning one’s back on the Day of Judgment. Marching, and slandering chaste believing women.”"
"10848","I am Muhammad bin Ibrahim, we are Al-Fadl bin Al-Ala, we are Othman bin Hakim, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out one afternoon, and he found them talking in their gatherings at the doors of the houses, so he said: “ What are these gatherings? Beware of these mounts where you sit. The houses, so we can stand out and talk. He said: “Then give the gatherings their right.” They said: What is their right, O Messenger of God? He said: “Lowering the gaze, speaking well, returning greetings, and guiding the astray.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10849","I am Muhammad bin Hatim, I am Hibban, I am Abdullah, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Nafi’, who said: I heard Al-Hasan bin Muslim speaking, on the authority of Safiyya bint Shaybah On the authority of Aisha, she said: “When this verse was revealed: And let them draw their veils over their pockets, she said: The women took their loincloths. So they tore it apart at the edges, and sealed it with it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10850","I am Muhammad bin Muammar, we are Hammad bin Masada, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, on the authority of Qais, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace When he got up at night to pray, he, peace and blessings be upon him, would say: “O God, You are the supremacy of the heavens and the earth, and to You belongs all praise. You are the light of the heavens and the earth. To You belongs all praise, You are the Lord of the heavens and the earth and whoever is in them. To You belongs praise, You are the Truth, Your word is the truth, Your promise is true, and meeting You is the truth. And the Hour is true, and the Fire is true. O God, to You I have submitted, and in You I have believed, and to You I have judged, and with You I have disputed, and to You I turn, so forgive me for what I have done. I have come forward and I have come back, and I have neither concealed nor declared, and you are my God. There is no god but You.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10851","I am Al-Hasan bin Muhammad, from Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Abu Al-Zubayr told me that he heard Jabir saying: “The calamity of a nation has come.” To some of the Ansar, she said: “My master is forcing me into prostitution, so God Almighty revealed: And do not force your girls into prostitution.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10852","I am Muhammad bin Salamah, I am Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa bin al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abd al-Qari He said: I heard Omar ibn al-Khattab saying: I heard Hisham ibn Hakim ibn Hazzam reciting Surat al-Furqan in a manner other than how I recited it to him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited it to me, so I almost hastened on him, then I gave him time until he left, then I wrapped him in his robe. So I brought him to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I heard this man reciting Surat Al-Furqan in a different manner. Did you read it to me? Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “Read.” So he recited the reading that I heard him reciting, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “This is how it was revealed.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “Read.” So I read, and he said: “This is how it was revealed. This is The Qur’an was revealed in seven letters, so recite as much as is possible.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10853","I am Al-Hussein bin Mansour, we are Hussein bin Muhammad, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, that a man said: O Messenger of God, how will he be gathered? People on their faces? He said: “Indeed, He who made them walk on their feet is able to make them walk on their faces.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10854","I am Hanad bin Al-Sirri, in his hadith, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked He asked: Which sin is greater? He said: “To make God a rival while He created you.” I said: Then what? He said: “You kill your child so that he may eat with you.” I said: Then what? He said: “That you commit adultery with your neighbour’s wife.” Abdullah said: Then God revealed the confirmation of that: And those who, with God, do not call upon any other god and do not kill “The soul which God has forbidden, except in truth, and do not commit adultery, and whoever does that will meet with sins.”"
"10855","I am Amr bin Ali, from Yahya, Sufyan told us, he said: Mansour and Suleiman told me, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abu Maysara, on the authority of Abd God, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, which sin is the greatest? He said: “That you make a rival to God while He created you.” I said: Then what? He said: “Then you kill your son in order for him to eat with you.” I said: Then what? He said: “Then you commit adultery with your neighbor’s girlfriend.”"
"10856","I am Al-Hasan bin Muhammad, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Al-Qasim bin Abi Bazza told me that he asked Saeed bin Jubayr: Is it for whom? He killed a believer intentionally out of repentance? He said: “No,” so he recited this verse: “And those who call upon no other god with God and do not kill the soul that God has forbidden except in the truth.” Sa’id said: I read it to Ibn Abbas, and he said: This is Meccan, and it was abrogated by a verse in Surat An-Nisa.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10857","I am Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, from Muhammad, from Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Abd al-Rahman ordered me to ask Ibn Abbas, regarding these two verses: “And whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell.” He said: “Nothing has abrogated it,” and regarding this verse: And those who do not call upon any other god with God and do not kill a soul that God has made sacred except in a just way. He said: It was revealed about the people of polytheism. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10858","I am Ahmad bin Sulaiman, we are Yazid bin Harun, I am Dawud, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Qur’an was sent down en masse to the heavens.” This world in the Night of Decree, then it was sent down after that in twenty years.” He said: “And they will not bring you an example unless We have brought you the truth and what is best.” An explanation, and a recitation, and a Qur’an which We have divided into parts so that you may read it to the people over a period of time, and We have sent it down as a final revelation.”"
"10859","Qutayba bin Saeed narrates, Jarir narrates, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Salama bin Qais, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said In the Farewell Pilgrimage, he said: “But they are only four, and I am not more stingy about them than I have been since I heard them from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Do not associate anything with God, and do not kill the soul that God has forbidden, except in the truth.” Hamza said: This means: And do not commit adultery, and do not steal."
"10860","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, from Amr, meaning Ibn Muhammad, from Sufyan al-Thawri, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu al-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Ibn Masoud said: “The oppression and brutality of the day of Badr passed, and the smoke, the moon, and the Romans passed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10861","I am Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah. My father told me. Ibrahim bin Tahman told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abu Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, Abraham saw his father on the day The Day of Resurrection will be covered with dust and dirt, so he said to him: I forbade you from doing this and you disobeyed me. He said: But today I will not disobey you for a single time. He said: i.e. My Lord, You promised me that You would not disgrace me on the day they are resurrected. If You disgrace his father, then you have disgraced the furthest. He said: O Abraham, I have forbidden it to the disbelievers. So it was taken from him, and he said: O Abraham, where is your father? He said: You took it from me. He said: Look down from it. He looked and saw Dhikh wallowing in it. It stinks, so he was taken by his feet and thrown into the Fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10862","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Abu Muawiyah, this is Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: When this verse was revealed: And warn Your closest clan. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Fatima, daughter of Muhammad, O Safiyya, daughter of Abd al-Muttalib, O Banu Abd Al-Muttalib, I am of no use to you before God at all, ask me of my wealth whatever you wish.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10863","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Jarir, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umayr, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: When it was revealed: And warn your closest clan. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called the Quraysh, and they gathered together. He made general and specific statements, and said: “O Banu Ka’b bin Luay O Banu Murrah bin Ka’b, O Banu Abd Shams, O Banu Abd Manaf, O Banu Hashim, save yourselves from the Fire, and O Banu Fatima, save yourself from the Fire, for I do not possess anything for you from God, except that you have a uterus, and I will wet it with my wetness.”"
"10864","I am Ahmad bin Suleiman, from Muawiyah bin Hisham, from Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: When it was revealed “And warn your nearest and dearest family.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood at Safa and said: “And it was two mornings.”"
"10865","I am Amr bin Ali, Yahya and Yazid bin Zurayi told us, they said: Al-Taymi and Al-Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Qubaisa bin Mukhariq and Zuhayr bin Amr said: When this verse was revealed: And warn your closest kindred, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, concluded May God bless him and grant him peace. He went to a ridge of a mountain and set a stone on top of it. Then he said: “O Banu Abd Manaf, I am only a warner. Your example is like a man who saw the enemy and went to meet his family. He was afraid that they would outrun him and return to his family, so he started shouting: “O morning!” \""
10866"""
"10866","Hannad ibn al-Sarri (said): from Abu al-Ahwas, from Furat, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah ibn Usayd, who said: We were conversing in the shade of a chamber of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). We mentioned the Hour (the Day of Judgment), and our voices rose. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) overlooked us from his chamber and said: ""What are you asking about? Or what are you discussing?"" We said: ""Mention of the Hour."" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The Hour will not come—or will not be established—until ten signs appear before it: the rising of the sun from its west, the emergence of the Beast (al-Dabbah), the emergence of Ya'juj and Ma'juj (Gog and Magog), the Dajjal (Antichrist), 'Isa ibn Maryam (Jesus son of Mary), the Smoke (al-Dukhan), and three landslides (khasf): a landslide in the East, a landslide in the West, and a landslide in the Arabian Peninsula. And the last of that will be a fire that emerges from the depths of 'Aden."""
"10867","I am Ubayd Allah bin Saeed, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Al-Tamimi, on the authority of Aslam, on the authority of Bishr bin Shaghaf, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, a Bedouin asked The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said about the pictures, and he said: “A horn that is blown into.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10868","I am Ali bin Hajar, I am Issa, and he is Ibn Yunus, on the authority of Hamza al-Zayat, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ali bin Mudarrak, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, “And you were not beside the mountain when we called out, saying: It was called out: O nation of Muhammad, I gave you before you asked me, and I answered you.” \before you invite me\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"10869","I am Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, our name is Muhammad, meaning Ibn Thawr, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of his father, he said: When Abu Talib was present at the time of his death. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon him, and Abu Jahl and Abdullah bin Abi Umayyah were with him, and he said: “Any uncle, Say: There is no god but God, a word with which I will plead with you with God.” Then Abu Jahl and Abdullah bin Abi Umayyah said to him: O Abu Talib, Do you renounce the religion of Abdul Muttalib? They did not stop talking to him, until he said the last thing he spoke to them: following the religion of Abdul Muttalib. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I will ask forgiveness for you for what I have done.” I have not forbidden you.” Then it was revealed: “It is not for the Prophet and those who have believed to ask forgiveness for the polytheists,” and it was revealed: “Indeed, you shall not guide whom you love.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10870","I am Al-Hasan bin Muhammad. Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr bin Dinar informed me, on the authority of Abu Sa’id bin Rafi’, that he said To Ibn Umar: “Is it from Abu Talib that the verse was revealed: ‘You shall not guide whom you love?’ He said: ‘Yes’.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10871","I am Al-Hasan bin Muhammad. Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Abi Mulaika informed me, he said: Amr bin Shuaib said, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, and he did not hear it from him, that it was Al-Harith bin Amir bin Nawfal who said: “If we follow guidance with you, we will be snatched from our land.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10872","I am Abu Dawud. He said: From us is Ali bin Ubaid, from us is Sufyan Al-Asfari, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in his saying: “Indeed, the one who made it obligatory You must recite the Qur’an when you return to Ma’ad. He said: To Mecca."
"10873","I am Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Uthman bin Omar, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: They were the People of the Book They read the Torah in Hebrew, then they explain it in Arabic to the people of Islam. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not believe the people of The Book, and do not disbelieve in them, but say: We believe in what was revealed to us, and it was revealed to you, and our God and your God are one, and to Him we submit. \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"10874","I am Shuaib bin Yusuf, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Fitr, he said: Muslim told me, on the authority of Masruq, he said: I heard Abdullah, saying: “They went on: “Batasha, and the darkness, and the rum, and the smoke, and the moon.”"
"10875","I am Al-Hussein bin Harith, I am Muawiyah bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Amra, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the Almighty’s saying: “M {1} defeated the Romans {2}. He said: It defeated, and it was defeated. The polytheists would love for you to appear.” Persia over the Romans, and the Muslims wanted the Romans to prevail over Persia because they were People of the Book, so they mentioned to Abu Bakr, so Abu The firstborn of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “But they will be defeated.” Abu mentioned him. Bakr, may God be pleased with him. So they said: Set a term between us and you. If we appear, we will have such-and-such, and if you appear, we will have such-and-such. And so on, he set a period of five years."
"10876","I am Ali bin Khashram, I am Isa, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: When it was revealed: “Those who believe and do not They cloak their faith with injustice. This is difficult for the Muslims. They said: O Messenger of God, who among us does not oppress himself? He said: “It is not that It is polytheism. Did you not listen to what Luqman said to his son: “O my son, do not associate anything with God. Verily polytheism is a great injustice.”"
"10877","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Ja’far bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “ If you hear a rooster crow, ask God for His bounty, for it has seen an angel. And if you hear a donkey braying, seek refuge in God from Satan, for she saw Satan.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10878","I am Ibrahim bin Yaqoub, he said: Muhammad bin Al-Sabbah told me, he said: Abu Ubaidah Al-Haddad told us, he said: Al-Akhdar bin Ajlan told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj al-Makki, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took my hand and said: O Abu Hurairah, “Indeed, God created the heavens and the earth and all that is between them in six days, then He ascended to the Throne on the seventh day, and created the dust on the Saturday, and the mountains on the Sunday, the tree on Monday, the perfection on Tuesday, the light on Wednesday, the animals on Thursday, and Adam on Friday in The last hour of the day after the afternoon, and He created the surface of the earth, its red and its black, its good and its bad. For that, God made “Glory be to Him, from the good and the bad Adam.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10879","I am Muhammad bin Bashar, we are Yahya bin Saeed, we are Sufyan. And I am Amr bin Ali, from Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite in the morning prayer on Friday: Al-M {1} The revelation of the prostration, and “Has it come?”, the wording. For Amr (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10880","I am Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Muhammad bin Thawr, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, who said: I was with the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. I became close to him as we were walking, and I said: O Prophet of God, tell me about an action that will bring me into Paradise and keep me far away. Regarding Hell, he said: “You have asked about a great matter, and it is easy for whomever God has made it easy for him: you establish prayer, pay zakat, and fast Ramadan.” And perform Hajj to the House.” Then he said: “Shall I not guide you to the gates of goodness? Fasting is a shield, and charity extinguishes sin as water extinguishes fire, and prayer.” The man from the middle of the night.” Then he recited: “Their sides should turn away from their beds,” until: “They recite Surah Al-Sajdah 16-17.” Then he said: “Shall I not inform you? At the head of the matter, its pillar, and its peak? I said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: The head of the matter: Islam, and its pillar: prayer, and its peak? Its hump means jihad. Then he said: “Shall I not tell you the meaning of all that?” I said: Yes, O Messenger of God, so he took hold of his tongue and said: “Stop this for you.” I said: O Messenger of God, are we held accountable for what we speak? He said: “May your mother be bereaved of you, O Muadh. Is there anything that topples people on their faces, or he said: on their noses, into Hell-fire other than the harvests of their tongues?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10881","“I am Amr bin Ali, from Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah,” And We will certainly make them taste the lesser torment, apart from the greater torment. He said: “Years have afflicted them.”"
"10882","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, Ya’qub told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, that he used to say: “We did not call on Zayd ibn Haritha except Zayd ibn Muhammad, until it was revealed in the Qur’an: Call them by their fathers. This is fairer in the sight of God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10883","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Musa bin Uqba told me that Salim bin Abdullah He told him, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Zaid bin Haritha, the client of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “We used to call him no one but Zaid bin Muhammad.” , until it was revealed: “Call them to their fathers.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10884","Harun bin Ishaq informed us, on the authority of Abdah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, “When they came to you from above you and from lower than you, and when the eyes became astray and the hearts reached the throats, they said: That is the Day of the Trench."
"10885","Qutaibah bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, who said: I heard Abu al-Hubab Sa’id bin Yasar say: I heard Abu Kitten, he says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I was ordered to go to a town that devours towns. They say: Yathrib, and it is the city that banishes people.” Just as furnace removes impurities from iron.”"
"10886","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, used to say: “There is no god but God alone. He strengthened His soldiers, supported His servant, and defeated the parties alone, and there is nothing after Him.”"
"10887","Al-Haytham bin Ayyub told us, he said: Ibrahim told us, Ibn Shihab said, on the authority of Kharijah, that his father, he said: “I missed a verse from Surah Al-Ahzab When we copied the Qur’an, I was hearing the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, reciting it, and I found her with Khuzaymah bin Thabit: from The believers are men who are true to what they covenanted with God, so I added it to its surah in the Qur’an.”"
"10888","Abdullah bin Al-Haytham told me, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah and Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Thabit Al-Bunani, on the authority of Anas, said: “Anas bin al-Nadir, by whom I was named, was absent from me. He did not bear witness with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He witnessed Badr, and he said: The first scene that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, witnessed. I was absent from it. By God, if God makes me witness a witness. With the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to see what I would do, so he was afraid to say something else, so when the following year he witnessed Uhud, he said: Then Saad bin Muadh met him and said: Muhayim. So he said to him: O Abu Amr, I feel the fragrance of Paradise rather than anyone else. So he fought until he was killed, and he was found. He had eighty-one marks, stab wounds, and blows. His sister said: I did not know my brother except by his appearance, and he was of good build. So she went downstairs. This verse: “Among the believers are men who were true to what they covenanted with God, without change.” So we believed that it was revealed about him and his companions."
"10889","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Humayd informed us, on the authority of Anas: “His uncle, he was absent from... Fighting, the people of Badr. When it was the day of Uhud and the Muslims were exposed, he said: Oh God, I apologize to you for what these people, meaning their companions, have done. And I disavow before you what these people brought, meaning the polytheists. Sa’d met him and not anyone else. Sa’d said: I was not able to do what he did. He said: Eighty stab wounds were found on him, including a stab with a spear, a blow with a sword, and a shot with an arrow. He said: So we used to say about him, and in His companions: “And among them are those whose lives have passed away, and among them are those who are waiting, and they have not changed anything.”"
"10890","I am Muhammad bin Hatim, na Suwayd, I am Abdullah, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that she said To the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “O Prophet of God, why do I hear men mentioned in the Qur’an, and women not mentioned?” Then God Almighty revealed: “Indeed, the Muslim men and Muslim women, the believing men and believing women.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
